.TH RM 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
rm \- remove files and directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rm
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.IR path ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rm
removes each file named. A symbolic link is removed itself, never what it
points to. A directory is removed only with
.BR \-r .
.SH OPTIONS
Options may be combined
.RB ( \-rf )
and may come anywhere among the paths.
.TP
.B "\-r \-R"
Remove directories and everything in them. Links inside are removed,
never followed.
.TP
.B \-f
Say nothing about paths that do not exist.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if everything named was removed (or, with
.BR \-f ,
was not there); 1 otherwise, or for an unknown option.
.SH NOTES
Any other option letter is refused (status 1, nothing removed). Any word
starting with
.B \-
is taken as options, so a file whose name starts with
.B \-
must be named as
.BR ./\-name .
There is no
.B \-i
(no prompting).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rmdir (1),
.BR mv (1),
.BR find (1)
